  "grafo_evidencia": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7f05a112-30dc-51d2-95ad-a1e8416a8d63",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Rhodesia, Northern Rhodesia, Southern Rhodesia, Zambia, Zimbabwe, Zambezi\n- People: Cecil Rhodes\n- Companies: British South Africa Company, BSAC\n- Organizations: British government\n- Concepts: British imperialism, protectorates\n\nFacts:\n- In 1895, the British South Africa Company named the southern African territory of Rhodesia after Cecil Rhodes.\n- Cecil Rhodes was an ardent believer in British imperialism.\n- Cecil Rhodes and the British South Africa Company founded the southern African territory of Rhodesia, which is now Zimbabwe and Zambia.\n- From 1924, the British government administered Northern Rhodesia as a protectorate under conditions similar to other British-administered protectorates.\n- From 1924, the special provisions that had applied when BSAC administered Northern Rhodesia were terminated.\n- The territory north of the Zambezi was officially designated Northern Rhodesia by the British South Africa Company.\n- Zambia has been the name of Northern Rhodesia since 1964.\n- The territory south of the Zambezi was dubbed Southern Rhodesia by the British South Africa Company.\n- Southern Rhodesia became Zimbabwe in 1980.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "eb81f082-f736-54f8-8dc8-c3342f7d9957",
        "text": "Page: Rhodesia (region). Sentence: The territory to the north of the Zambezi was officially designated Northern Rhodesia by the Company, and has been Zambia since 1964; that to the south, which the Company dubbed Southern Rhodesia, became Zimbabwe in 1980.\nPage: Northern Rhodesia. Sentence: From 1924 it was administered by the British government as a protectorate under similar conditions to other British-administered protectorates, and the special provisions required when it was administered by BSAC were terminated.\nPage: Cecil Rhodes. Sentence: An ardent believer in British imperialism, Rhodes and his British South Africa Company founded the southern African territory of Rhodesia (now Zimbabwe and Zambia), which the company named after him in 1895.",
